"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3763642086","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/115020#issuecomment-3763642086","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/115020","id":3763642086,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7gVJ7m","user":{"login":"BastiaanOlij","id":1945449,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5NDU0NDk=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1945449?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/BastiaanOlij","html_url":"https://github.com/BastiaanOlij","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BastiaanOlij/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BastiaanOlij/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BastiaanOlij/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BastiaanOlij/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BastiaanOlij/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BastiaanOlij/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BastiaanOlij/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BastiaanOlij/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BastiaanOlij/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-01-17T13:10:22Z","updated_at":"2026-01-17T13:11:25Z","body":"> @BastiaanOlij I looked at implementing compile-time `#ifdef USE_MULTIVIEW` as suggested, but it seems like that would require significant architectural change affecting multiple rendering subsystems.\r\n> \r\n> If you'd prefer to pursue the compile-time approach, I'm happy to explore it further, but it would be a much larger scope change.\r\n\r\nAh sorry if I wasn't clear enough, indeed we **currently** don't have a mechanism to expose built-in defines that aren't known until shader compilation. `USE_MULTIVIEW` is such a define. It would be the nicer solution however it will require far more work to make it possible to use such defines in user shader code (which is what StandardMaterial3D produces). After looking at how we've got this currently implemented in our shader preprocessor, this does not seem like an easy improvement.\r\n\r\nI'm not sure what the best way forward here is, I think the solution as is does the job, but I'm personally not happy about the extra if statement for behavior that is known at compile time. The overhead here is likely neglectable, and someone who really requires an optimisation can always convert the standard material to a shader material and remove the bit of code they don't need.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3763642086/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3770197301","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/115020#issuecomment-3770197301","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/115020","id":3770197301,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7guKU1","user":{"login":"BastiaanOlij","id":1945449,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5NDU0NDk=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1945449?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/BastiaanOlij","html_url":"https://github.com/BastiaanOlij","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BastiaanOlij/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BastiaanOlij/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BastiaanOlij/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BastiaanOlij/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BastiaanOlij/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BastiaanOlij/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BastiaanOlij/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BastiaanOlij/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BastiaanOlij/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-01-19T21:37:54Z","updated_at":"2026-01-19T21:37:54Z","body":"Ah, I missed we do have a solution for using defines but it works differently than I expected. Totally missed that clue when this was discussed.\r\n\r\nI'll put up a PR with the change so we hopefully can still include it in RC2.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3770197301/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3771742528","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/115020#issuecomment-3771742528","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/115020","id":3771742528,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7g0DlA","user":{"login":"akien-mga","id":4701338,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ3MDEzMzg=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/4701338?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga","html_url":"https://github.com/akien-mga","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_